        {
          "line": 29,
          "text": "{project_name} can implement OAuth Identity and Authorization Chaining Across Domains between two different realms or servers by combining the following supported features:"
        },
        {
          "line": 36,
          "text": "== Overview of the complete flow"
        },
        {
          "line": 44,
          "text": "== Step 1: Configure Token Exchange in `domaina`"
        },
        {
          "line": 50,
          "text": "=== 1.1 Create a client that represents `domainb`"
        },
        {
          "line": 63,
          "text": "=== 1.2 Create a client scope to grant access to `domainb`"
        },
        {
          "line": 84,
          "text": "NOTE: This example allows any user to request that client scope. Roles can be used to restrict the scope of the client scope. This way only users with a specific role would be allowed to add the `domainb` audience."
        },
        {
          "line": 86,
          "text": "=== 1.3 Create a client to perform the Token Exchange"
        },
        {
          "line": 103,
          "text": "=== 1.4 Create a sample user"
        },
        {
          "line": 108,
          "text": "=== 1.5 Test Token Exchange"
        },
        {
          "line": 124,
          "text": "Now `clienta` can exchange the token, including scope `access-domainb`, and restricting the audience to `http://localhost:8080/realms/domainb` (issuer of `domainb`)."
        },
        {
          "line": 144,
          "text": "== Step 2: Configure JWT Authorization Grant in `domainb`"
        },
        {
          "line": 150,
          "text": "=== 2.1 Create an OpenID Connect Identity Provider for `domaina`"
        },
        {
          "line": 166,
          "text": "=== 2.2 Create a client to perform the JWT Authorization Grant"
        },
        {
          "line": 179,
          "text": "=== 2.3 Link the sample user in `domainb`"
        },
        {
          "line": 181,
          "text": "To test the JWT Authorization Grant, the sample user created in `domaina` should be linked in `domainb`. You can just access to the account page in `domainb`:"
        },
        {
          "line": 187,
          "text": "* Check in **Account security** -> **Linked accounts** that the user is correctly linked to `domaina`."
        },
        {
          "line": 189,
          "text": "=== 2.4 Test JWT Authorization Grant"
        }
